! TCPIP$SERVICE.DAT -- TEST OVERLAY variant (rd vms-843a SSH cold-boot proof).
! Staged into a test build ONLY via --build-arg OVMX_TEST_ENABLE_SSH=1; the
! SHIPPED distro/rootfs SERVICE.DAT keeps every service DISABLED (SSH included --
! SSH-enable-by-default is an operator posture call, Baron-reserved).
!
! SSH is enabled here so the auxiliary server (TCPIP$INETD) binds :22 over the
! executive BGn: seam, ACP-stages SYS$SYSTEM:VMSSSHD.EXE (the wrapped OpenSSH
! sshd) off the ODS-2 system disk, and launches it in inetd mode (-i) on the
! accepted connection -- proving an inbound `ssh SYSTEM@` lands an authenticated
! DCL session (SSH -> SYSUAF -> DCL) end to end on the proven (B) aux-launch path
! (vms-21b). sshd -i reads/writes the accepted fd on stdin/stdout (dup2'd by the
! aux server); -f names the sshd_config the SSH overlay generated on the initramfs
! (HostKey + SYSUAF password auth). The privsep siblings sshd-session/sshd-auth
! live at the OpenSSH-baked /ovmxsshsrv/libexec (initramfs) -- see the Dockerfile
! SSH overlay.
!
!     service-name  port  image-filespec  [image-args...]
!
SSH 22 SYS$SYSTEM:VMSSSHD.EXE -i -f /ovmxsshsrv/etc/sshd_config
